THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS AND DATA
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product includes the open data and open-source software listed below; their
respective licenses govern those components. The corresponding license texts are
available in the project repository (and, where they ship with the app, under
public/).

Astronomy
  - Swiss Ephemeris — planetary positions (JPL DE441 data), via
    @swisseph/browser, the bundled fixed-star catalog (a 40-star extract
    of its sefstars.txt), and the hypothetical points' orbital elements (its
    seorbel.txt from version 2.10.03: every element line unchanged, some
    comment lines removed). © Astrodienst AG. Licensed AGPL-3.0.
    https://www.astro.com/swisseph/
  - JPL Small-Body Database — the orbit class behind each bundled minor
    planet's class tag. NASA/JPL-Caltech. https://ssd.jpl.nasa.gov/tools/sbdb_query.html
  - Five Millennium Catalogs of Solar and of Lunar Eclipses — the bundled
    eclipse catalogs (dates, types, Saros series). Eclipse Predictions by
    Fred Espenak and Jean Meeus (NASA's GSFC); reproduced with the required
    acknowledgment. https://eclipse.gsfc.nasa.gov

Maps & places
  - OpenStreetMap — base map data (also credited on the map itself).
    © OpenStreetMap contributors, ODbL.
    https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright
  - OpenFreeMap — free vector tiles, label fonts, and sprites.
    https://openfreemap.org
  - OpenMapTiles — vector tile schema.
    https://openmaptiles.org
  - OpenMapTiles styles — MapTiler Basic, OSM Bright, Dark Matter and
    Positron, some adapted. Code BSD-3-Clause, design CC BY 4.0.
    © MapTiler.com & OpenMapTiles contributors; © Mapbox; © CartoDB.
    The copy of MapTiler Basic redistributed in public/basemaps/ keeps its
    notice beside it (MAPTILER-BASIC-LICENSE.md).
    https://openmaptiles.org/styles/
  - GeoNames — offline place-name search and city lookup. CC BY 4.0.
    https://www.geonames.org
  - IANA Time Zone Database — the per-zone standard-time adoption dates
    bundled as lmtEras.json (see scripts/build-lmt-table.mjs), used to cast
    pre-standard-time births in the birthplace's local mean time.
    Public domain. https://www.iana.org/time-zones
  - Natural Earth (via the world-atlas package) — country boundaries.
    Public domain. https://www.naturalearthdata.com

Type & software
  - Noto Sans Symbols & Noto Sans Symbols 2 — astrological glyphs.
    SIL Open Font License 1.1. © 2022 The Noto Project Authors.
    https://github.com/notofonts/symbols
  - MapLibre GL JS — interactive map rendering. BSD-3-Clause.
    https://maplibre.org
  - mapbox-gl-rtl-text — right-to-left text on the map (Arabic shaping and
    joining, Arabic and Hebrew in reading order). BSD-2-Clause.
    © 2017 Mapbox. https://github.com/mapbox/mapbox-gl-rtl-text
  - ICU (International Components for Unicode) — the shaping and
    bidirectional-text code compiled into mapbox-gl-rtl-text. Unicode license.
    © 1991-2016 Unicode, Inc. https://icu.unicode.org
  - React, Turf.js, Luxon, tz-lookup, and other dependencies — see package.json;
    most are MIT-licensed.

